{
  "_comment": [
    "Slash-command ownership for the v3 TUI: the one place it is declared (plan H-5, 2026-10-18).",
    "Read by src/commands/catalog-manifest.ts (slash.ts, wave-intercepts.ts) and by r4/src/r4/companion/ui/slash_manifest.py (list_slash_commands).",
    "owner: local = v3 handles every form of the line, except forwardVerbs (sent to the companion intact) or, when localVerbs is given, every verb not listed there;",
    "       bare-local-args-forward = the bare command runs in v3, any args form goes to the companion intact;",
    "       forward = v3 keeps only metadata, the line goes to the companion.",
    "Verbs are the first argument token, lower-case; \"\" is the bare command.",
    "intercept: the first dispatch stage that claims the name: wave (wave-intercepts.ts), builtin (dispatchBuiltinVerbs), owned (OWNER_OWNER_VERBS), pane (handleWorkflowPane), managed (dispatchManagedVerbs), catalog (the row's localRun).",
    "aliases: the v3 row's aliases (list_slash_commands never exports them). canon: alias -> args prefix; the alias is rewritten to the row's name before any stage sees it.",
    "interceptAliases: names the intercept stage also serves that stay companion aliases. forwardAs: companion command a forwarded line names (default: the row's name).",
    "companionRow: omit = list_slash_commands leaves the companion row out; ignore = v3 drops the companion row when merging. slashRow false = dispatch-only name (no v3 catalog row).",
    "ignoresArgs: the local handler takes no arguments, so typed args are dropped by design (every owner-local catalog row: its localRun gets none). /clear also sends the bare /clear on.",
    "save (K1.6, 2026-10-24): dispatch-only (the companion's /save row lists it); bare runs in v3; the wave table's 'save *' row also keeps a turn-shaped args form local (/save 2, /save t2 mine, /save --vouch); any other args form (a transcript path) goes to the companion intact.",
    "tests/slash-reachability.test.ts dispatches every Python registry command, alias and subcommand against this file."
  ],
